{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FrPA86HPf1NyBrW8ZYopKJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1-#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2:# Build the Gate-K unit test (host CUDA). Run: ./build/gate_units ref/goldens\n3-set -e\n4-cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n5-\n6-# Gate TOPK_RADIX — the single-CTA radix select (DECODE_LADDER 1.2) must be BIT-IDENTICAL to the warp\n--\n35-# Gate INDEX_SCORE (DECODE_LADDER 1.5) -- `index_score` now has FOUR implementations and TWO\n36-# separate bit-exactness claims: IXS_TILED == IXS_WARP (memory placement only) and IXS_GEMM ==\n37:# IXS_SCALAR (the reference order the warp kernel walked away from in Finding 68). gate_units next\n38-# door is a COSINE gate against the golden and would pass a reduction-order change; this is memcmp,\n39-# and it also PRINTS the deviation IXS_GEMM spends against the shipped warp kernel per input\n40-# distribution, so the number behind the LOSSLESS gate is measured and not asserted.\n41-nvcc -O2 -std=c++17 -gencode arch=compute_110a,code=sm_110a -I include \\\n--\n45-echo \"built build/gate_index_score\"\n46-\n47:# `kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu` ADDED HERE 2026-08-20 (DECODE_LADDER 1.5). It was missing, so gate_units\n48-# had not LINKED since nvfp4 landed -- and because this line is a bare `nvcc` under `set -e`, the\n49-# whole script died here and NONE of the twelve gates below it rebuilt either. That is the failure\n50-# mode the \"THE OTHER EIGHT\" block at the bottom of this file was written to prevent, reappearing\n51-# above the block it was written in: `bg` records failures and keeps going, the raw `nvcc` lines up\n52-# here do not. Found by 1.5 running the script, not by reading it.\n53-nvcc -O2 -std=c++17 -gencode arch=compute_110a,code=sm_110a -I include \\\n54:  tests/gate_units.cu kernels/fp8_block_gemm.cu kernels/hc_sinkhorn.cu kernels/mla_attn.cu kernels/moe.cu kernels/hc.cu kernels/compressor.cu kernels/indexer.cu kernels/tc_moe_gemm.cu kernels/tc_fp8_gemm.cu kernels/dscratch.cu kernels/dprof.cu kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu \\\n55:  -o build/gate_units\n56:echo \"built build/gate_units\"\n57-# CPU-only gates (no GPU): chat encoder byte-exactness + OpenAI API shaping.\n58-g++ -O1 -std=c++17 -I include tests/gate_encoding.cpp -o build/gate_encoding && echo \"built build/gate_encoding\"\n59-nvcc -O3 -std=c++17 -gencode arch=compute_110a,code=sm_110a -I include tests/gate_bf16w.cu kernels/compressor.cu kernels/dscratch.cu kernels/mla_attn.cu kernels/indexer.cu kernels/fp8_block_gemm.cu kernels/tc_fp8_gemm.cu kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu -o build/gate_bf16w && echo \"built build/gate_bf16w\"\n60-g++ -O1 -std=c++17 -I include tests/gate_api.cpp      -o build/gate_api      && echo \"built build/gate_api\"\n--\n74-  tests/gate_ogroup_gemv.cu kernels/mla_attn.cu kernels/dscratch.cu kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu -o build/gate_ogroup_gemv\n75-echo \"built build/gate_ogroup_gemv\"\n76:# Gate TC_FP8_SMEM — the smem-staged FP8 tensor-core GEMM (Finding 41). gate_units checks\n77-# tc_fp8_gemm at ONE (M,N,K); this sweeps every shape and every M the verify path issues, plus the\n78-# N%64 and M%16 tails that the tile mapping gets wrong independently of each other.\n79-nvcc -O2 -std=c++17 -gencode arch=compute_110a,code=sm_110a -I include \\\n80-  tests/gate_tc_fp8_smem.cu kernels/fp8_block_gemm.cu kernels/tc_fp8_gemm.cu kernels/dscratch.cu kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu -o build/gate_tc_fp8_smem\n--\n86-# `compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck` too: that is what found the shared over-read.\n87-nvcc -O2 -std=c++17 -gencode arch=compute_110a,code=sm_110a -I include -lineinfo \\\n88:  tests/gate_prefill_len.cu kernels/compressed_decode.cu kernels/compressed_attn.cu kernels/compressor.cu \\\n89-  kernels/indexer.cu kernels/mla_attn.cu kernels/mla_forward.cu kernels/mla_decode.cu kernels/hc.cu \\\n90-  kernels/hc_sinkhorn.cu kernels/fp8_block_gemm.cu kernels/tc_fp8_gemm.cu kernels/dscratch.cu kernels/dprof.cu \\\n91:  kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu -o build/gate_prefill_len\n92:echo \"built build/gate_prefill_len\"\n93-# Gate MOE_SCAN — the parallel MoE grouping scans (k_moe_prefix_par / k_build_tiles_par) must be\n94-# BIT-IDENTICAL to the <<<1,1>>> kernels they replaced. Equality, not cosine: these are integer\n95-# scans. Sweeps nr below/at/above the 256-thread block width plus empty, exactly-16 and multi-tile\n96-# experts, because per LEVERS.md trap 9 a harness that cannot express the regime confirms itself.\n--\n116-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n117-# THE OTHER EIGHT (Finding 76). Before this block, build_gate.sh built 10 of the 18 gate binaries\n118:# and the rest went stale SILENTLY: F74 found gate_compressed_decode and gate_indexer_decode a day\n119-# out of date, and gate_fp4_gemv turned out to be two engine parameters behind — it had not linked,\n120-# and therefore had not tested anything, since F65/F72 added `rows_hint`/`align8`, while a binary\n121-# from 2026-08-06 sat in build/ looking like a passing gate. A gate that is not in the build script\n122-# is a gate that measures the past. Sources are listed here rather than in each file's header\n--\n139-FULL=\"$CDEC kernels/mla_forward.cu kernels/mla_decode.cu kernels/hc.cu kernels/hc_sinkhorn.cu \\\n140-  kernels/moe.cu kernels/tc_moe_gemm.cu\"\n141:for t in gate_compressed_decode gate_indexer_decode; do bg $t $CDEC; done\n142:for t in gate_scratch_init gate_compressed_graph gate_indexer_graph; do bg $t $FULL; done\n143-bg gate_compressor_emit kernels/compressor.cu kernels/mla_attn.cu kernels/indexer.cu \\\n144-  kernels/dscratch.cu kernels/fp8_block_gemm.cu kernels/tc_fp8_gemm.cu kernels/nvfp4_dense.cu\n145-# moe.cu, for `fp4_gemm` — the oracle this gate diffs the grouped GEMV against. Its own header build\n146-# line lists only tc_moe_gemm.cu and has not linked since the oracle moved.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b702730-b205-4592-87e9-ff91aade6c17","uuid":"eda1a107-cc8a-4162-ad15-83062083c6a5