{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeE9dmqQGmjC7jHbAg51D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GYTou9ot8copTYgR14xM21","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p5.txt <<'MSG'\n1.5: index_score as a register-tiled GEMM -- +4.57 % tok/s at ctx 12,410, and the context term\nfalls 0.572 +/- 0.018 ms per 1000, which is 89 % of what 0.4 predicted for this mark\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED. One server load per arm, control (warp kernel) arm FIRST so drift favours the\ncontrol, four reps x three sweep contexts plus two control contexts:\n\n  ctx    ms/forward before -> after   paired    tok/s before -> after    tau\n  3,197  142.94 -> 141.45             -1.49     12.14 -> 12.27 (+0.99 %) 1.736 both\n  6,260  146.95 -> 143.76             -3.19     11.87 -> 12.15 (+2.24 %) 1.788 both\n 12,410  154.44 -> 147.77             -6.67     10.46 -> 10.93 (+4.57 %) 1.615 both\n\nAll 16 legs faster. tau, mean verify width and the EMITTED TEXT HASH identical in every one, at\nctx up to 12,410 -- not at ctx 9. Regressing the 16 paired deltas on context:\n\n  delta_fwd = +0.358 +/- 0.134  -0.5724 +/- 0.0178 x (ctx/1000)    R^2 0.987, n=16\n\nWHAT IT MEANS. 0.4 attributed 0.644 +/- 0.018 ms per 1000 to the `i:score` mark. This delivered\n0.572 +/- 0.018 -- prediction and delivery agree inside one SE, which is the strongest thing this\nladder has said about its own cost model. The tracked b goes 2.514 -> 1.942 (b x 6592: 16.57 ->\n12.80 ms; stop wants <= 5.0), carried by SUBTRACTING a paired number rather than re-fitting a\nnarrow range, because over ctx 3,197-12,410 the arms fit b to R^2 0.701 and 0.433. Cumulatively b\nis down 73 % from the 7.220 the ladder opened on. Note the intercept: at zero context the GEMM is\n0.358 +/- 0.134 ms SLOWER, break-even near ctx 625 -- and on build/decode at seqmax 85 it is a\nmeasured NULL (21.03-21.24 vs the warp kernel's 21.02-21.26, tau 2.87 in all six replicates,\ngenerated ids byte-identical). A change worth +4.6 % where the kernel has rows and nothing where it\ndoes not is behaving like a context-term change, which is the claim.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, and the part worth remembering. The shipped warp kernel re-read both operands from\nglobal on every head: 1.2 GB moved per call at the verify shape to do 151 M MACs, 0.5 FLOP/byte.\nAn intermediate tiled kernel fixes exactly that and is bit-identical to the shipped kernel -- and\nthat capped it at 2.0x, because bit-exactness with the warp kernel mandates keeping its 5-step\n__shfl_down_sync tree, and SHFL is a ~200 us floor at this shape however the operands are staged.\nThe GEMM is bit-identical to index_score_kernel, the SCALAR REFERENCE gate_units checks against\nref/goldens, because register-tiled accumulation in k IS the reference's order -- and it is 6.8x.\n\"Bit-exact\" is a two-place relation and the second argument is a design decision; claiming it\nagainst the incumbent inherits every reassociation the incumbent ever made, including (Finding 68)\nones adopted as explicit deviations.\n\nTHE INVARIANT, second branch. Not bit-exact with what it replaces, so it ships behind the LOSSLESS\ngate with the deviation MEASURED: gate_index_score sweeps 1130 shapes / 21,773,760 floats at 0\ndiffering on both claims, and prints what the change spends vs the warp kernel per distribution\n(up to 88 % of elements differ, max_abs 4.88e-04, max_rel 0.847 on near-zero scores). Those are\nmeaningless alone -- the kernel feeds a SELECTION -- so the evidence that counts is the 16/16\nbyte-identical texts at context above. LOSSLESS GATE PASS x3; gate_units, gate_indexer_decode,\ngate_compressed_decode, gate_prefill_len rc=0; both CUDA-graph capture gates bit-identical.\n\nA GATE THAT DOES NOT COMPILE IS A GATE THAT PASSES BY NEVER RUNNING. Phase 1 could not start:\ngate_indexer_decode, gate_compressed_decode, gate_indexer_graph and gate_compressed_graph had not\nbuilt since 5c1e047 split x_full into (x_cur, x_full) and left four test call sites one argument\nshort. That is the entire in-situ correctness harness for the subsystem items 1.2-1.5 all edit,\nabsent for the whole ladder to date, on top of the set -e + bare-nvcc breakage iteration 7 found in\nbuild_gate.sh one line above it. Fixed, and all four pass.\n\nWiki: kernel-optimisations.md 2.7 (the win), negative-results.md 4d (the 2x version and why the\nreference choice cost 3.4x), context-scaling.md (the term; three of 0.4's four items are now spent\nand what is left is not linear), measurement-and-traps.md 20 (a gate has three outcomes and only\ntwo are ever printed) and 21 (dprof reads a saving 15-20 % low: attribute with it, ratchet with the\nclean pair), README.md state table.\nMSG\nwc -l evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p5.txt; grep -n \"COMMIT_MSG\" scripts/decode_loop.sh | head","description":"Write the commit message for the driver"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1283,"cache_read_input_tokens":170558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1283},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b702730-b205-4592-87e9-ff91aade6c17","uuid":"3a7abd2c-655e-49a3-af75-f73874ab2dc6","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:22:21.905Z","request_id":"req_011CeE9dkEexeHETm79x2rsP"}
