oduces byte-identical generated     token ids, or ships behind the LOSSLESS gate with the deviation measured and written down. If     you cannot show which, REVERT rather than keep it.   * REPORT tau IN EVERY A/B. A byte-identical token sequence can still collapse acceptance from     3.12 to 1.00, because acceptance is an exact draft/target comparison. Throughput without tau is     not a measurement.   * NEVER restart the eval battery, re-enable its systemd units, or modify the checkpoint.   * Do not change clock settings unless the ladder item IS the clock change.   * One change per measurement. Report bands, not points. The run-to-run spread is 3.5%.  When done: update DECODE_LADDER.md (mark the item, add what you measured), commit with a message that states what was measured and what it means, and push. If the item cannot be completed, say so in the ladder entry and leave it unchecked rather than faking progress.  This is iteration 8. The topmost unchecked ladder item is: 745:- [ ] **1.5** **CONFIRMED BY 0.4, 2026-08-20 — this kernel is 9 % of the context term.** --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format stream-json --verbose\n=== mem ===\n               total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available\nMem:             122          17         104           0           2         105\n=== git ===\n M DECODE_LADDER.md\n M DECODE_ZENITH_FINDINGS.md\n M evidence/decode_loop/build_1p5_gate.log\n M evidence/decode_loop/driver.log\n M evidence/decode_loop/gate_tokenizer.log\n M evidence/decode_loop/gate_topk_warp.log\n M evidence/decode_loop/live.log\n M evidence/memguard.log\n M scripts/ixgemm_ab_run.sh\n M tests/gate_compressed_decode.cu\n M tests/gate_compressed_graph.cu\n M tests/gate_indexer_decode.cu\n M tests/gate_indexer_graph.cu\n M wiki/README.md\n M wiki/context-scaling.md\n M wiki/kernel-optimisations.md\n M wiki/measurement-and-traps.md\n M wiki/negative-results.md\n?? evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p5.txt\n?? evidence/decode_loop/bu