{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeE9juTxKQTXwvDcGNZAX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 8 complete — ladder item **1.5** is done, measured, gated, and written up.\n\n## What shipped\n\n`index_score` — the DSA indexer's row scorer, run once per ratio-4 layer every forward — is now a register-tiled GEMM instead of a warp-per-(query,row) kernel. The old kernel re-read both operands from global on every head (32 KiB of `q` once per row, `kv[t]` once per head): **1.2 GB moved per call at the verify shape to do 151 M MACs, 0.5 FLOP/byte**.\n\n## The ratchet (paired, same session, control arm first)\n\n| ctx | ms/forward → | paired Δ | tok/s → | τ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3,197 | 142.94 → 141.45 | −1.49 | 12.14 → **12.27** (+0.99 %) | 1.736 both |\n| 6,260 | 146.95 → 143.76 | −3.19 | 11.87 → **12.15** (+2.24 %) | 1.788 both |\n| 12,410 | 154.44 → 147.77 | −6.67 | 10.46 → **10.93** (+4.57 %) | 1.615 both |\n\nAll 16 legs faster; `tau`, verify width and the **emitted text hash identical in every one**. Regressing the 16 paired deltas: **−0.572 ± 0.018 ms per 1000 context**, R² 0.987 — **89 % of the 0.644 ± 0.018 that item 0.4 predicted for this mark.** Tracked `b` goes 2.514 → 1.942 by subtraction (not re-fit — this sweep's range determines `b` at R² 0.43). `i:score` itself: 0.503 → 0.040 ms/1000, and 6.58 ms at ctx 12,288 reproduced 0.4's number exactly.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**The win came from re-aiming the bit-exactness claim.** The first version was bit-identical to the *shipped* kernel and that capped it at 2.0× — bit-exactness with the warp kernel mandates keeping its `__shfl_down_sync` tree, which is a ~200 µs floor at this shape. Claiming it against the *scalar reference* instead (whose serial-in-k order is what a register-tiled GEMM already does) gives 6.8×. Written up in `negative-results.md` §4d.\n\n**Four in-situ gates had not compiled since commit `5c1e047`** — `gate_indexer_decode`, `gate_compressed_decode`, and both CUDA-graph capture gates, i.e. the entire in-situ harness for the subsystem items 1.2–1.5 all edit. Fixed (one missing argument each, from the `xin`-ring split) and all four now pass at `maxabs 0.00e+00`. `measurement-and-traps.md` §20.\n\nInvariant satisfied on its second branch: not bit-exact with what it replaces, so `gate_index_score` measures the deviation (1130 shapes / 21.77 M floats / 0 differing against the reference; up to `max_rel` 0.847 against the incumbent) and the downstream evidence is the 16/16 byte-identical texts at context. LOSSLESS gate PASS ×3, τ 2.87 both arms, and the decode binary at ctx 85 is a clean null — worth nothing where the kernel has no rows, which is what a context-term change should look like.\n\nLadder, `DECODE_ZENITH_FINDINGS.md`, and five wiki pages updated; `COMMIT_MSG_1p5.txt` is staged for the driver to commit and push. GPU is idle, 105 GiB free, nothing left running."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1886,"cache_read_input_tokens":182631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1886},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b702730-b205-4592-87e9-ff91aade6c17","uuid":"eb448a91-bac8-4b77-9ca9-20b4939d51ea","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:23:36.980Z","request_id":"req_011CeE9jtHGAcsVWeeEZpQq8"}
